# What each setting in scripts/set-variables does (#2181): NAME|short line|detail.
# Plain words. The short line shows in the list, the detail when a setting is picked.
# Where .env.example or docs/DEPLOY.md already explain a setting, the wording comes from there.
# A test checks that every setting the menu lists has a line here.
DISCORD_DEV_GUILD_ID|Your test server, for instant command updates|Optional, for development. DMbot always registers its commands for every server. If you put your private test server's ID here (right-click the server, Copy Server ID, with Developer Mode on), the commands are also copied to it so changes show up at once. The catch: in that one server every command appears twice. Empty: off. Needs a restart.
DISCORD_CLEAR_GUILD_COMMANDS|Servers whose old duplicate commands are removed|A one-time cleanup. List server IDs, separated by commas, and at the next start DMbot removes the old per-server copy of its commands there, so they stop showing every command twice. Remove the value after one start. Empty: nothing is cleaned.
DATABASE_POOL_MAX|Most database connections DMbot holds open|The most connections DMbot keeps open to the database. Default 10. Raise it for a busy bot. If you run several copies of DMbot, give each about 4, so all together stay under the database's own limit. Needs a restart.
EARS_WS_HOST|Where the voice and main parts talk (leave)|The local address of the link between the voice part (ears) and the main part (core). Default 127.0.0.1, which means only this computer. Leave it unless you know why. Needs a restart of both.
EARS_WS_PORT|Door number they talk through (leave at 8765)|The port (door number) of the local link between the voice part (ears) and the main part (core). Default 8765. Change it only if another program already uses that port; ears and core must use the same one. Needs a restart of both.
TRANSCRIBER|Which service turns speech into text|whisper-local (the default) runs free on this computer. deepgram is pay as you go and needs no graphics card (needs DEEPGRAM_API_KEY). cloud is any OpenAI-compatible service. none writes no text at all. With deepgram or cloud, players' voices and Discord names are sent to that company: the consent message says so, and people who agreed before the switch are asked again. Needs a restart (docker compose up -d).
TRANSCRIBE_LANGUAGE|Language people speak|A language code such as en, es or de, or auto to let the service detect it. Default en. A wrong language makes the text much worse. Needs a restart.
TRANSCRIBE_WORKERS|How many clips are turned into text at once|How many clips are written at once, for different servers (each server's clips stay in order). Empty: 1 for whisper-local, which fills the processor, and 3 for deepgram and cloud. More is faster only if the machine or the service can take it. Needs a restart.
WHISPER_MODEL|Size of the free local speech model|Used only with TRANSCRIBER=whisper-local. On a processor-only server use base or small. With a graphics card use large-v3 or turbo. Bigger is more accurate and slower. Default small. Needs a restart.
WHISPER_DEVICE|Whether the local model uses processor or graphics card|Used only with whisper-local. auto (the default) picks the graphics card when there is one. You can force cpu or cuda. Needs a restart.
WHISPER_COMPUTE_TYPE|Speed setting of the free speech model (leave at auto)|Used only with whisper-local. auto (the default) picks the right setting for your machine. Change it only to fix a compatibility problem. Needs a restart.
WHISPER_BEAM_SIZE|Accuracy versus speed of the free model (1 = fastest)|Used only with whisper-local. 1 (the default) is fastest. Higher is a little more accurate and slower. Needs a restart.
CLOUD_STT_URL|Web address of the cloud speech service|Used only with TRANSCRIBER=cloud: the /audio/transcriptions address of any OpenAI-compatible service. Default is OpenAI's (leave unless you use another company). Players' voices are sent there. The key is set with scripts/set-key CLOUD_STT_API_KEY. Needs a restart.
CLOUD_STT_MODEL|Model name asked of the cloud speech service|Used only with TRANSCRIBER=cloud. The model the service should use. Default whisper-1. Needs a restart.
DEEPGRAM_MODEL|Deepgram model|Used only with TRANSCRIBER=deepgram. Empty uses the default, nova-3. Needs a restart.
DEEPGRAM_LISTEN_URL|Deepgram address the bot sends voice to|Used only with deepgram. Empty uses the usual address, https://api.deepgram.com/v1/listen. Change it only if Deepgram gives you another. Needs a restart.
SPEECHMATICS_URL|Speechmatics address for the comparison tool|Only the speech-to-text comparison tool uses this; the bot never does. Empty means the US address, wss://us.rt.speechmatics.com/v2. Set it only if your Speechmatics portal shows a different real-time address for your account (for example with eu in it). It must start with wss://.
DEEPGRAM_URL|Deepgram address for the comparison tool|Only the speech-to-text comparison tool uses this (it must start with wss://); the bot uses DEEPGRAM_LISTEN_URL instead. Empty means wss://api.deepgram.com/v1/listen.
AI_MODEL_FAST|AI model for the simple, cheap jobs|The Claude model for simple jobs: cleaning the transcript, the off-topic filter, finding names, rules lookups and quick answers for DMs. A small, cheap model. The default is right. The value must start with claude- (no quotes or spaces). If it is unavailable DMbot quietly uses another and notes it once in the log. Costs money per use. Needs a restart.
AI_MODEL_CAREFUL|AI model for house-rule changes|The Claude model for changes to house rules: a middle model. The default is right. The value must start with claude-. If it is unavailable DMbot uses the next cheaper one and notes it once in the log. Costs money per use. Needs a restart.
AI_MODEL_DEEP|AI model for story planning|The Claude model for the strongest, most expensive work. Today only the story extractor uses it, and only when DMBOT_STORY_EXTRACTOR_TIER is deep. The default is right. The value must start with claude-. Needs a restart.
AI_MODEL_CREATIVE|AI model that writes the recap|The Claude model that writes the recap as plain text. Default is the strongest model. The value must start with claude-. Costs money for every recap. Needs a restart.
AI_MODEL_FORMATTING|AI model that shapes the recap into sections|The Claude model that shapes the recap text into sections without changing a word. A small model is enough. The value must start with claude-. Needs a restart.
DMBOT_ADMIN_PRIMARY_ID|Who is told when the AI account runs dry|A Discord user ID (17 to 20 digits). That person is messaged privately when the AI account runs out of money or reaches its monthly limit, at most once a day. Empty: nobody is messaged, it is only logged. Find an ID with Developer Mode on, then right-click the person and Copy User ID.
DMBOT_ADMIN_SECONDARY_ID|Backup person told when the AI account runs dry|The same as the first admin, a second person, messaged in case the first can't be reached, when the AI account runs out of money or hits its limit (at most once a day). Empty: no backup.
SHARD_COUNT|Split DMbot into parts (leave at 1)|Leave this at 1 unless DMbot is in a few thousand servers. Discord can split a bot's servers into parts (called shards); one part is right until then. The voice service and core must use the same number, or core refuses to start. Default 1. Needs a restart of both.
SHARD_IDS|Which part this copy runs (leave empty)|Comma separated part numbers (shards) this copy of DMbot serves. Empty means all of them. For example with SHARD_COUNT=4, one copy running on its own uses 0,1 and another uses 2,3. Needs a restart.
LOG_FORMAT|How the log is written|text (the default) is easy to read. json writes one line per event, for log-reading tools. Logs hold IDs only, never names, what people said, or keys. Needs a restart.
LOG_LEVEL|How much the log says|INFO (the default) is the usual. DEBUG says much more and is only for tracking a problem. WARNING says less. Needs a restart.
MEMORY_CHANGELOG_KEEP_DAYS|Days that Undo works on names and connections|After each session, older undo history for campaign memory is deleted so it does not grow forever. This is how many days Undo works. Whole days, 1 or more. Default 30. Applies from the next session end.
COMPOSE_PROFILES|Extra services Docker starts, like the website API|Set to web to start the website's API container as well. Leave empty until the website goes live. Changing it needs docker compose up -d.
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID|Discord app ID for website sign-in|The Client ID of your Discord app (Developer Portal, your app, OAuth2). The website's sign-in with Discord uses it. Empty: customer sign-in is off. Needs a restart of the website API.
WEB_SITE_URL|Address of the website|The website's public address, https. It must be on the same site as WEB_API_URL (for example https://dmbot.example). DMbot's messages send people there to buy or manage plans. Needs a restart of the bot and the website API.
WEB_API_URL|Address of the website's API|The API's public address, https, on the same site as WEB_SITE_URL (for example https://api.dmbot.example). In the Discord Developer Portal, your app, OAuth2, add this address plus /auth/discord/callback under Redirects. Needs a restart of the website API.
WEB_SESSION_DAYS|Days a website sign-in lasts|How many days a person stays signed in, 1 to 90. Default 30. Longer is more convenient and a little less safe. Applies to new sign-ins after a restart of the website API.
PAYMENT_PROVIDER|Which company takes payments|Type stripe to take payments. Empty: buying says payments are off. fake is for testing on your own computer only. Needs a restart of the website API.
STRIPE_PRICE_TABLE|Stripe Price for the one-table plan|The Price ID (starts price_) in the Stripe dashboard for the one-table plan. Used when PAYMENT_PROVIDER=stripe. Empty: that plan cannot be bought. Needs a restart of the website API.
STRIPE_PRICE_TWO_TABLES|Stripe Price for the two-table plan|The Price ID (starts price_) in the Stripe dashboard for the two-table plan. Empty: that plan cannot be bought. Needs a restart of the website API.
STRIPE_PRICE_GUILD|Stripe Price for the Guild plan|The Price ID (starts price_) in the Stripe dashboard for the Guild plan. Empty: that plan cannot be bought. Needs a restart of the website API.
STRIPE_PRICE_EXTRA_HOURS|Stripe Price for the extra 10 hours|The Price ID (starts price_) in the Stripe dashboard for the +10 extra hours. Empty: extra hours cannot be bought. Needs a restart of the website API.
STRIPE_PRICE_RECAP_AUDIO|Stripe Price for the narrated-recap add-on|The monthly Price ID (starts price_) of the recap audio add-on. Leave empty until it exists: the add-on is then not for sale and its button stays hidden (Guild has audio anyway). Needs a restart of the website API.
STRIPE_MANAGED_PAYMENTS|Let Stripe act as the seller (1 = yes, 0 = no)|1 asks Stripe to be the seller (Managed Payments). Accept Stripe's terms in the Stripe dashboard first. Leave 0 until a test purchase has been checked. Needs a restart of the website API.
GITHUB_FEEDBACK_REPO|Where the website's Say hello messages go|The GitHub repository the Say hello forms post to, as owner/name. Empty means smv620/Discord-DMbot. It needs Discussions turned on and two categories named exactly Feedback and Questions. The token is set with scripts/set-key GITHUB_FEEDBACK_TOKEN.
SUPPORT_TEAM_EMAIL|Address told when a support ticket waits|One address that is emailed when a support ticket is waiting. The email holds the ticket's subject and the conversation so far. Empty: tickets are still kept and shown on the admin page, and nobody is emailed. Needs the SMTP settings. Needs a restart of the website API.
WEB_CLIENT_IP_HEADER|Where your proxy puts the visitor's address|The header that the service in front of your website (Cloudflare) puts the visitor's address in, for the one-message-per-10-minutes limit: CF-Connecting-IP behind Cloudflare. Needed when GITHUB_FEEDBACK_TOKEN is set, except on localhost. The API must then be reachable only through that service, or anyone could pick their own address. Needs a restart of the website API.
SMTP_HOST|Mail server DMbot sends email through|Empty means nothing is ever sent. With Resend: smtp.resend.com. With Gmail: smtp.gmail.com. Sign-in links, move codes and the Try It and support emails all go through it. The password is set with scripts/set-key SMTP_APP_PASSWORD. Needs a restart.
SMTP_PORT|Mail server port|The mail server's port. Default 587, which is right for Resend and Gmail. Needs a restart.
SMTP_USER|Mail server user name|With Resend this is the word resend. With Gmail it is the Gmail address. Needs a restart.
MAIL_FROM|From address on every email|The From address on emails DMbot sends. With Resend: DMbot <accounts@getdmbot.com>. DMbot refuses admin@getdmbot.com for any From address. Support emails fall back to this if their own is empty. Needs a restart.
MAIL_SUPPORT_FROM|From address of support emails|What people receive about their support question, for example DMbot support <info@getdmbot.com>. Their replies come back to it. Empty: MAIL_FROM is used. Needs a restart of the website API.
MAIL_ALERTS_FROM|From address of alerts to the team|The sender of alerts to the team (SUPPORT_TEAM_EMAIL). The real address is private; see docs/EMAIL.md. Empty: MAIL_FROM is used. Needs a restart of the website API.
OWNER_ALERT_EMAIL|Owner's private address for failure alerts|One short email goes here when the AI, Deepgram, Stripe, mail or the database fails. It is private: set it only here on the server, never in the repository, an issue or a chat. Empty: no alert emails (the log says so once).
MAIL_ALERTS_REPLY_TO|Optional Reply-To on owner alert emails|An optional Reply-To address on the owner's alert emails, for example an ops address. Empty: none.
MAIL_REPLY_DOMAIN|Where people's emailed replies to support go|A plain domain name (for example reply.getdmbot.com) that only the mail service receives, because the main domain's mail goes to the team's inboxes. Empty: the domain of the support address. Needs a restart of the website API.
SUPPORT_AI_MODEL|AI model for the support helper|The Claude model that answers support questions first. Empty: the strongest tier's current default. It uses ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, so the website API needs that key too. Costs money per answer. Needs a restart of the website API.
MAIL_POSTAL_ADDRESS|Postal address printed on offer emails|US law asks for a postal address at the bottom of offer emails (the trial-end and extension ones). They are not sent while this is empty. Type a vertical bar for a line break.
MAIL_DAILY_CAP|Most emails sent in one day|Keep it at or under your mail provider's daily limit (Gmail about 500; for Resend read the free limit on its dashboard). Default 400. Emails past it wait. Needs a restart.
ADMIN_EMAILS|Who may sign in to the admin page|The only email addresses that may sign in to /admin, separated by commas. Empty: the admin sign-in is off. Needs a restart of the website API.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID|Google app ID for admin sign-in|The Client ID of your Google app for signing in to the admin page. The address Google sends people back to is WEB_API_URL plus /admin/auth/google/callback. Empty: only the admin password works. The secret is set with scripts/set-key GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET.
DMBOT_DEBUG_AUDIO|Log audio health per utterance|1 makes the voice service log audio health for each utterance (user IDs and packet counts only, no audio). Default 0. Only for tracking a voice problem. Needs a restart of ears.
DMBOT_ENFORCE_PLANS|Check plans and hours|0 (the default): DMbot records everyone's listening hours but never refuses a start or warns about hours. 1: it checks the owner's plan and hours at /dmbot start and warns the DM as hours run low. Turn it on only once people can pay on the website. Needs a restart of the bot and of the website API.
DMBOT_IMPORTS|Website import of older sessions|0 (the default): importing is hidden and shows "not found" for everyone. 1 turns importing on, once a real import has been checked. Needs a restart of the website API.
DMBOT_SIDEBAR|DM quick answers|0 (the default): a DM's voice messages and typed questions get the reply "Quick answers aren't switched on yet." 1: they are answered (needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY). Costs a little per answer. Turn it on only after the test answers have been read. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_TIME_SUGGESTIONS|Offer a time jump from vague narration|1 lets the DM screen offer a [+2 hours] button when narration probably passes time but no strict phrase matches. The clock never moves by itself. It sends the DM's one line and the game time to the smallest AI model, at most 20 calls a session for a campaign, on paid plans only. 0: off, nothing calls the AI. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_STORY_EXTRACTOR|Read each session for story facts|1 reads every session after it ends and proposes what was said for the DM to confirm. This calls the AI a lot and costs money. 0 (the default): off, not shown to customers. Keep it off until its prompt passes the measurement in docs/costs.md. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_LIVE_HEADS_UP|Live heads-up when a dead character is voiced|1 shows a heads-up on the DM screen, while a session runs, when a character you confirmed as dead is voiced at the table. No AI. 0 (the default): off, until the live check at the test table. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_LIVE_HEADS_UP_MINUTES|Minutes between two live heads-ups|0 to 120. Default 5. Only matters when DMBOT_LIVE_HEADS_UP is 1. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_STORY_EXTRACTOR_TIER|AI tier that reads the transcript|fast, careful or deep. Default fast. A stronger tier reads better and costs more. Only matters when the story extractor is on. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_STORY_EXTRACTOR_MAX_CALLS|Most AI calls one session may make|From 1 to 5000. Default 480. A cap on the story extractor's cost for one session. Only matters when the extractor is on. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_STORY_EXTRACTOR_MAX_CALLS_DAY|Most AI calls one campaign may make in a day|From 1 to 50000. Default 960, two sessions' worth. A daily cap on the story extractor for one campaign. Only matters when the extractor is on. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_CLEANER_RANK_MAX|Most did-they-mean ranking calls per session|For the Did they mean... questions, one fast AI call per question puts the most likely name first, marked likely. It never changes a line; the DM still answers. This is the most calls a session makes. Default 40. 0 turns ranking off. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_CONTINUITY_POSSIBLE|How sure DMbot must be to say "possible"|A number from 0 to 1 (0.25 means 25% sure). Default 0.25. It sets the word possible in continuity warnings. Leave it unless a test says otherwise. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_CONTINUITY_PROBABLE|How sure DMbot must be to say "probable"|A number from 0 to 1 (0.5 means 50% sure). Default 0.5. It sets the word probable in continuity warnings. Leave it unless a test says otherwise. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_CONTINUITY_LIKELY|How sure DMbot must be to say "likely"|A number from 0 to 1 (0.8 means 80% sure). Default 0.8. It sets the word likely in continuity warnings. Leave it unless a test says otherwise. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_CONTINUITY_MIN_FACTS|Confirmed facts needed before any warning|How much confirmed story a campaign needs before any continuity warning is shown. Default 50 facts. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_CONTINUITY_MIN_SESSIONS|Sessions needed before any warning|How many sessions a campaign needs before any continuity warning is shown. Default 3. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_THREAD_STALLED_SESSIONS|Sessions before a story thread counts as stalled|A thread that is hinted, open or going on is called stalled when this many sessions have started since it last moved. The after-session report says how many are. Default 3. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_RECALL_BUDGET|How much story each helper may read|The most characters of the campaign's story that one helper (the ones that track names and plot, and the DM quick answers) is handed at a time. Smaller is faster and cheaper; larger remembers more. Default 4000. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_FREE_USERS|Discord accounts that use DMbot free|Discord user IDs, separated by commas, that use DMbot with no hours or campaign limits: the owner's own. Never put real numbers in the repository, only here. Needs a restart of both the bot and the website API.
DMBOT_TEST_RECORDING_GUILDS|Test servers allowed to keep voice files|Empty (the default): DMbot never saves anyone's voice. On the TEST server only, list its server number here. Then people who press Save my voice for tests have their voices kept as files on DMbot's own computer, only to re-check that DMbot still works. They are never published, never in the database or a backup, and are deleted after 7 days unless a session is marked to keep. Stop saving my voice deletes a person's files at once. Needs a restart of core.
DMBOT_TEST_RECORDINGS_DIR|Folder for saved test voices|Where the test voice files go inside the core container (a volume, owner-only). The default is right for docker compose. Needs a restart of core.
DMBOT_SIDEBAR_RECALL|Quick answers use the confirmed story|1 (the default): the DM sidebar's quick answers use what the DM has confirmed about the story, for the audience players (no secrets, no notes), each cited by the AI and checked in code. 0: off, the prompt is exactly the old one. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_SIDEBAR_RECALL_BUDGET|Story characters one quick answer may add|200 to 4000, default 1000: how many characters of confirmed story one question may add to a quick answer. More costs a little more. Needs a restart of the bot.
DMBOT_RECAPS|Cinematic recaps after each session|1 writes an in-world previously-on recap after a session and emails the DM when it is ready. The DM reads, edits and posts it on the website; nothing reaches the table unless they press Post. Costs AI money per recap. 0 (the default): off until the first real-session check. Only for campaigns whose plan includes story memory. Needs the mail settings and WEB_SITE_URL. Needs a restart of the bot.
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID|Narrator's voice for spoken recaps|The ElevenLabs voice ID of the narrator. With no voice or no key the recap is made text-only and nothing fails. Does nothing until DMBOT_RECAPS is 1. The key is set with scripts/set-key ELEVENLABS_API_KEY.
ELEVENLABS_SPEECH_MODEL|Voice model for spoken recaps|The ElevenLabs voice model. Default eleven_v3, which understands the delivery tags. Change it only after comparing by ear. Costs credits per recap.
DMBOT_RECAP_AUDIO_MAX_CREDITS|Most voice credits one recap may use|A cap on the ElevenLabs credits for one recap. Default 15000. About 7000 is usual. A recap that would use more is made text-only instead.
DMBOT_RECAP_VOICE_TAGS|Mood cues reach the narrator's voice|1 (the default): the recap's mood cues (tense, somber, hopeful) reach the voice as delivery tags, once where the mood changes. 0: only whisper, sigh and pauses, so a narration can be compared by ear.
DMBOT_RECAPS_PER_MONTH|Most recaps one campaign may make a month|Counted per calendar month in UTC, to keep the bill under what a plan earns. Default 10. A Try again counts; a failed job does not. Free access and grants are not limited. Past it the DM screen says when the next one is.
DMBOT_RECAP_AUDIO_PER_MONTH|Most narrated recaps one campaign may make a month|Counted per calendar month in UTC. Default 8. A Try again counts; a failed job does not. Free access and grants are not limited. Past it the recap is text-only and the DM screen says when the next one is.
DMBOT_PRESESSION_NOTE|Note on the DM screen when a session starts|1 (the default): shows the last recap, what is open about names heard last time, what was lost or ended, and how many things said at the table wait to be checked. Built from what the DM confirmed, no AI call; only for plans with story memory. 0: off. Needs a restart of the bot.
